* Behavioural 4-pole transistor-ladder lowpass ("tanh" ladder model).
*
* This is NOT a vendor model of the SSI2144 (none is published). It is the
* standard large-signal ladder approximation: four gm-C stages whose
* transconductors saturate as tanh(v / 2Vt), with resonance as negative
* feedback k from the output to the input stage. It is used to study gain
* structure (level vs distortion), the passband loss caused by resonance,
* and resonance compensation. Calibration against the SSI2144 datasheet
* (Rev 3.0): input clips around +-50 mV, nominal level +-20 mV, oscillation
* at a loop gain of 4 (12 dB of feedback). See README.md for limits.
*
* Ports:  in  = differential input voltage at the chip pins (V)
*         out = ladder output, unity DC gain at k = 0
* Params: fc  = cutoff frequency (Hz)
*         k   = resonance feedback (0 = none, 4 = self-oscillation)

.subckt ladder4 in out params: fc=1k k=0
.param vt=25.85m cst=1n
.param ifc={fc*4*3.14159265*vt*cst}
* stage 1 (input stage, sees input minus feedback)
B1 0 n1 I={ifc*(tanh((V(in)-k*V(n4))/(2*vt)) - tanh(V(n1)/(2*vt)))}
C1 n1 0 {cst}
R1 n1 0 1G
B2 0 n2 I={ifc*(tanh(V(n1)/(2*vt)) - tanh(V(n2)/(2*vt)))}
C2 n2 0 {cst}
R2 n2 0 1G
B3 0 n3 I={ifc*(tanh(V(n2)/(2*vt)) - tanh(V(n3)/(2*vt)))}
C3 n3 0 {cst}
R3 n3 0 1G
B4 0 n4 I={ifc*(tanh(V(n3)/(2*vt)) - tanh(V(n4)/(2*vt)))}
C4 n4 0 {cst}
R4 n4 0 1G
Eout out 0 n4 0 1
.ends ladder4
